  "note": "Automation tier of every scan finding id (ROADMAP P15, 2026-09-26). finding-stats groups mods by their hardest remaining tier; revive decides what it may apply and what becomes an escalation packet from this table. Ids with a computed part use {...} as in docs/CHECKS.md. A test fails when a scan finding id has no tier here, so a new check must be placed. Moving an id out of 'mechanical' means writing its fixer (see fixers.SUPPORTED_FINDINGS).",
  "tiers": {
    "none": "Nothing to do: the game accepts it, or it is evidence for another check.",
    "auto": "A fixer exists and needs nothing beyond the target version, vanilla core or the finding itself.",
    "input": "Needs a value only the owner can give (a design type, a bay count, a role, a description); where a fixer exists it applies the value.",
    "mechanical": "Deterministic, but no fixer exists yet: the best candidates for new fixers.",
    "decision": "An owner or policy decision (dependency, licence, content choice); tooling applies it once made.",
    "code": "Needs source changes that take judgement: escalate to AI with a packet, verify with BridgeForge.",
    "inspect": "Unreadable or unverifiable input: look at it first; usually small once seen."
  },
